{"schema_version":1,"course":"tourist-sv","unit":"emergencies-and-health","language":"en","target_language":"sv","phrases":[{"concept":"help","text":{"Latn":"Help!"}},{"concept":"call-the-police","text":{"Latn":"Call the police!"}},{"concept":"call-an-ambulance","text":{"Latn":"Call an ambulance!"}},{"concept":"i-need-a-doctor","text":{"Latn":"I need a doctor"}},{"concept":"where-is-the-pharmacy","text":{"Latn":"Where is the pharmacy?"}},{"concept":"where-is-the-hospital","text":{"Latn":"Where is the hospital?"}},{"concept":"i-feel-sick","text":{"Latn":"I feel sick"}},{"concept":"please-help-me","text":{"Latn":"Please help me"}},{"concept":"stop-thief","text":{"Latn":"Stop, thief!"}},{"concept":"it-hurts-here","text":{"Latn":"It hurts here"}}],"glosses":[{"lemma":"sv:hjalp","gloss":"help"},{"lemma":"sv:ringa","gloss":"to call, to phone"},{"lemma":"sv:polis","gloss":"police","note":"“Polisen” (“the police”) takes the ending “-en”. “Polis” alone is a police officer."},{"lemma":"sv:en","gloss":"a, an; one","note":"Swedish has two genders: “en” for most words (en kaffe) and “ett” for the rest (ett glas). Learn each noun with its article."},{"lemma":"sv:ambulans","gloss":"ambulance"},{"lemma":"sv:jag","gloss":"I","note":"“Mig” is the object form: “Hjälp mig” (help me)."},{"lemma":"sv:behova","gloss":"to need"},{"lemma":"sv:lakare","gloss":"doctor"},{"lemma":"sv:var","gloss":"where"},{"lemma":"sv:vara","gloss":"to be","note":"“Är” is the present tense for every person: jag är, du är, det är."},{"lemma":"sv:apotek","gloss":"pharmacy"},{"lemma":"sv:sjukhus","gloss":"hospital"},{"lemma":"sv:maa","gloss":"to feel (well or ill)","note":"“Jag mår illa” means “I feel sick” (nausea); “Jag mår bra” means “I'm well”."},{"lemma":"sv:illa","gloss":"badly, ill"},{"lemma":"sv:hjalpa","gloss":"to help"},{"lemma":"sv:tack","gloss":"thank you; please","note":"Means “thank you”, and after a request also “please”: “En kaffe, tack.”"},{"lemma":"sv:stoppa","gloss":"to stop"},{"lemma":"sv:tjuv","gloss":"thief"},{"lemma":"sv:det","gloss":"it, that"},{"lemma":"sv:gora","gloss":"to do, to make","note":"“Det gör ont” (it hurts) is literally “it does hurt”."},{"lemma":"sv:ont","gloss":"pain, hurt"},{"lemma":"sv:har","gloss":"here","note":"“Det här” is “this”, literally “the here”."}]}
